  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Centre for Integrated Mountain Dev. (ICIMOD), 2017-2022 - International Centre for Integrated Mountain Dev. (ICIMOD), 2017-2021</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">International Centre for Integrated Mountain Dev. (ICIMOD), 2017-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ICIMOD har ans&#xf6;kt om st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida uppg&#xe5;ende till 150 MSEK f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;rande av ICIMOD:s program i regionen Hindu Kush Himalaya enligt planen  &quot;Medium Term Action Plan,  2018-2022&quot;. ICIMOD &#xe4;r en mellanstatlig organisation som genom regionalt samarbete utvecklar och delar kunskap f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja h&#xe5;llbar utveckling i regionen. Organisationens medlemsl&#xe4;nder &#xe4;r Afganistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Kina, Indien, Myanmar, Nepal och Pakistan.  ICIMOD:s program bidrar till  minskad fattigdom, minskad fysisk och social s&#xe5;rbarhet samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttring av ekosysemtj&#xe4;nster f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;n, kvinnor och barn i regionen. Det svenska bidraget ges som ett  programst&#xf6;d  i syfte att harmoniera st&#xf6;det s&#xe5; l&#xe5;ngt m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r ett effektivt genomf&#xf6;rande av fem&#xe5;rsplanen. Programst&#xf6;det innefattar st&#xf6;d till regionala program, innovation och integration samt till institutionella funktioner. Det svenska st&#xf6;det samfinansieras med andra givare.
 
Planerade strategiska resultat &#xe4;r:
- Spridning av innovationer och praxis som utvecklats av ICIMOD och partners f&#xf6;r anpassning till f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar som leder till positiva resultat f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;n, kvinnor och barn. T ex &#xf6;versv&#xe4;mningsvarningssystem och klimatanpassade v&#xe4;rdekedjor.
- Betydande framsteg i generering och anv&#xe4;ndning av relevant data, kunskap och analys. T ex m&#xe4;ta, bevaka och hantera luftf&#xf6;roreningsniv&#xe5;er.
- Betydande framsteg i tillv&#xe4;gag&#xe5;ngss&#xe4;tt och kunskap som st&#xf6;djer j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och inkluderande utveckling. T ex st&#xe4;rka kvinnors kapacitet och ledarskapsroller inom jordbruk och lokala beslutsfattande institutioner.
- Betydande framsteg i m&#xe4;nsklig- och institutionell kapacitet. T ex st&#xe4;rka medlemsl&#xe4;ndernas milj&#xf6;f&#xf6;rvaltning.
- Betydligt p&#xe5;verkade policyer genom ICIMOD och partnerorganisationers arbete. T ex bidra till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad milj&#xf6;lagstiftning i regionen.
- F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt regionalt samarbete relaterat till h&#xe5;llbar utveckling i bergsomr&#xe5;den. T ex fr&#xe4;mja tekniskt kunskapsutbyte mellan l&#xe4;nder och gemensam f&#xf6;rvaltning av gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande naturresurser.
- Global k&#xe4;nnedom om det aktuella bergsomr&#xe5;dets (Hindu Kush Himalaya) betydelse f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade och resilienta livsvillkor och ekosystem. T ex f&#xe5; genomslag i de globala klimatf&#xf6;rhandlingarna.

Det svenska bidraget ska finansiera slutf&#xf6;rande av den p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende fasen under 2017 samt ett brett programst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r ICIMOD:s fem&#xe5;rsplan 2018-2022. Finansiering av den nya fem&#xe5;rsplanen planeras ske med st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n 8 givare d&#xe4;r Sverige ing&#xe5;r. Dessutom kommer mindre belopp att tillhandah&#xe5;llas fr&#xe5;n de &#xe5;tta medlemsl&#xe4;nderna. ICIMOD beh&#xe5;ller ca 70 % av budgeten f&#xf6;r de regionala programmen och vidaref&#xf6;rmedlar ca 30 % till partnerorganisationer. Sverige har samarbetat med ICIMOD under l&#xe5;ng tid och har under perioden 2012-2016 finansierat tv&#xe5; av ICIMOD:s initiativ: Atmosf&#xe4;rinitiativet samt klimatanpassningsinitiativet HICAP.

ICIMOD ska enligt enligt f&#xf6;reslagna avtalsvillkor inkomma med &#xe5;rlig revision av tredje parts organisationer som f&#xe5;r medel &#xf6;verstigande 505 000 SEK. Avtalsutkast har tagits fram i n&#xe4;ra samarbete med JUR. 

Det milj&#xf6;ekonomiska forskningsn&#xe4;tverket SANDEE, som under 15 &#xe5;r med goda resultat st&#xf6;tts genom Sveriges Strategi f&#xf6;r Forskningssamarbete, integreras fr&#xe5;n 2017 med ICIMOD och f&#xe5;r h&#xe4;refter del av programst&#xf6;det till organisationen. P&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt kan synergier mellan forskning och regional utvecklingssamarbete nyttjas. Resultat kan &#xe4;ven forts&#xe4;ttningsvis rapporteras p&#xe5; och bidra till Forskningsstrategin. 

Vid sidan om, men kopplat till detta st&#xf6;d, kommer Sverige ocks&#xe5; att finansiera en Bitr&#xe4;dande Bilateral Expert (BBE) till ICIMOD, inom omr&#xe5;det vatten och klimatanpassning.

Beredningen &#xe4;r skriven p&#xe5; engelska eftersom nationell handl&#xe4;ggare bidragit i beredningarbetet och kommer att delta i uppf&#xf6;ljning av insatsen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICIMOD has applied for support from Sida amounting to 150 000 000 SEK for implementation of ICIMOD&apos;s operations in the Hindu Kush Himalayan region, according to the plan &quot;Medium Term Action Plan, 2018-2022&quot;. ICIMOD is an intergovernmental organization which through regional cooperation generates and shares knowledge to promote sustainble development in the region. The organization&apos;s member countries are Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, China, India, Myanmar, Nepal and Pakistan. The ICIMOD&apos;s programs contribute to reduced poverty, reduced physical and social vulnerability and improvement of ecosystem services for men, women and children in the region. The Swedish contribution is given as overall program support in order to harmonize the support as far as possible for the effective implementation of the five-year plan. Program support includes support for regional programs, - innovation and integration as well as institutional functions.
 
Planned strategic results are:
- Dissemination of innovations and practices developed by ICIMOD and partners for adaptation to changes that result in positive results for men, women and children. E.g.: flood early warning systems and climate change adapted value chains.
- Significant progress in the generation and use of relevant data, knowledge and analysis. E.g.: Measure, monitor and manage air pollution levels.
- Significant progress in approaches and knowledge supporting gender equality and inclusive development. E.g.: Strengthen women&apos;s capacity and leadership roles in agriculture and local decision making bodies.
- Significant progress in human and institutional capacity. E.g.: Strengthen the member countries&apos; environmental management authorities.
- Significantly affected policies through ICIMOD and partner organizations work. E.g.: contribute to improved environmental legislation in the region.
- Strengthened regional cooperation related to sustainable development in mountain areas. E.g.: promote technical exchange between countries and joint management of transboundary natural resources.
- Global awareness of the importance of mountain areas for improved and resilient living conditions and ecosystems. E.g.: influence at the global climate negotiations.

The Swedish contribution will fund the completion of the current phase in 2017 and a broad program support for ICIMOD&apos;s five-year plan 2018-2022. Funding of the new five-year plan is planned with support from 8 donors where Sweden is included. In addition, smaller amounts will be provided from the eight member states. ICIMOD retains approximately 70% of the budget for regional programs and transmits about 30% to partner organizations. Sweden is a longstanding cooperation partner of ICIMOD, and Sweden has during the period 2012-2016 financed two of ICIMOD&apos;s initiatives, the climate change adaptation initiative HICAP and the Atmosphere initiative.

ICIMOD performs annual audits of third party organizations that receive funds exceeding SEK 505,000.

The environmental economics network SANDEE, which has for 15 years been supported with good results under Sweden&apos;s Strategy for Research Cooperation, will from 2017 be integrated into ICIMOD and take part of Sweden&apos;s new programme support to ICIMOD. SANDEE&apos;s results will continue to contribute to the Research Strategy.

Sweden will also separately finance a Bilateral Associate Expert (BAE) position at ICIMOD, in the field of water and climate adaptation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICIMOD has seven strategic results guiding their work and outlined in their Strategy and Results Framework;

1) Widespread adoption of innovation and practices developed by ICIMOD and partners to adapt to change, leading to positive impacts for women, men and children.

2) Significant advances in the generation and use of relevant data, knowledge and analysis.

3) Significant advances made in approaches and knowledge that promote gender equality and inclusive development.

4) Significantly developed human and institutional capacity.

5) Policies considerably influenced by the work of ICIMOD and its partners.

6) Enhanced regional cooperation related to sustainable mountain development.

7) Global recognition of the importance of mountains to ensure improved and resilient livelihoods and ecosystems.


There are six regional programmes with specific outcomes;

1) Adaptation and Resilience Building

2) Transboundary Landscapes

3) River Basins and Cryosphere

4) Atmosphere

5) Mountain Environment and Regional Information Systems

6) Mountain Knowledge and Action Networks</narrative>
  </description>
